  "semantic_notes": [
    {
      "heading": "[ edit 8 19 Quick Notes ]",
      "text": "8 19 is the first non-obvious torus knot in the table - it is in fact T(4,3) . It is also the pretzel knot P(3,3,-2). [ edit 8 19 Further Notes and Views ] 8_19 is the first non-homologically thin knot in the Rolfsen table. (That is, it's the first knot whose Khovanov homology has 'off-diagonal' elements.) Knotscape Symmetrical form ; (3,4) torus knot True-lover's knot with sticked free ends Equal to the previous, from knotilus Pretzel knot P(2,-3,-3) French logo Seen in Singapore",
      "source": "rendered-text-window"
    },
